               BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

 IN THE MATTER OF SOUTHWESTERN PUBLIC                                    )
 SERVICE COMPANY’S APPLICATION FOR: (1)                                  )
 REVISION OF ITS RETAIL RATES UNDER ADVICE                               )   Docket No. 25-00079-UT
 NOTICE 341; AND (2) OTHER ASSOCIATED RELIEF                             )
                                                                         )

                      ORDER APPOINTING CO-HEARING EXAMINERS

          THIS MATTER comes before the New Mexico Public Regulation Commission

(“Commission”) upon Southwestern Public Service Company’s (“SPS”) Application for Authority

to Change Rates and for Other Approvals and Authorizations with Schedules A-1 through Q-6 (the

“Application”). The Commission appoints Hearing Examiners Patrick Schaefer and Christopher

Ryan to preside over this matter.

                                           BACKGROUND

          1.     On November 20, 2025, SPS filed the Application requesting authority to change

its base rates and certain other approvals. 1 Specifically, SPS requests to increase its base rate

charges for the New Mexico retail jurisdiction by $175,354,544, a 24.25% increase over current

base rate revenue and 16.73% in total revenues, based on a total New Mexico retail revenue

requirements of $892,652,373 for the Future Test Year running from December 1, 2026, through

November 30, 2027. 2 The Application includes a request for an overall weighted average cost of

capital of 8.21% for the Future Test Year, reflecting a 56% equity ratio, an authorized return on

equity of 10.5%, and a cost of debt of 5.29%. 3 The Application includes requests for several other

approvals, summarized in the 1600-page filing and in the testimonies of 29 SPS witnesses. 4



1 Application at 1.
2 Id. at 3.
3 Id.
4 This order summarizes relevant background. The full electronic record of this proceeding is available at

https://edocket.prc.nm.gov.
                                FINDINGS AND CONCLUSIONS

       2.       The appointment of Hearing Examiners Patrick Schaefer and Christopher Ryan will

provide for administrative efficiency and assist in the orderly and timely resolution of this matter.

       3.       The Commission may appoint hearing examiners to preside over this matter. 5

       IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       A.       Hearing Examiners Patrick Schaefer and Christopher Ryan are hereby appointed to

preside over this matter, take all action necessary and convenient within the limits of the Hearing

Examiner’s authority, conduct any necessary hearings, and take any other action in this case that

is consistent with law, including issuing a recommended decision.

       B.       This Order is effective when signed.

       C.       The Commission shall serve a copy of this Order upon all persons listed on the

attached Certificate of Service via e-mail if their e-mail addresses are known, and otherwise, via

regular mail.

       D.       In computing time in accordance with statute, regulation, or Commission order, the

computation shall begin on the date that this Order is filed with the Chief Clerk of the

Commission’s Records Management Bureau or the Chief Clerk’s designee.

       SIGNED under the Seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, this 25th day of

November, 2025.

                         NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

                         /s/ Gabriel Aguilera, electronically signed
                         GABRIEL AGUILERA, COMMISSIONER



5 See NMSA 1978, § 62-19-20 (2020); 1.2.2.29 NMAC.



